        <briefdescription>
<para>Simulates a network using the static explicit Ralston method of order 4. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Network</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Target network to simulate.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Time</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Duration of the simulation. Must be greater than zero.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Step</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Step size. Must be greater than zero.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Callback</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>External discrete callback called once at local simulation time of 0, then again after each integration step. May be NULL.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Returns NDXL_OK if _Network is successfully integrated over _Time, otherwise returns <ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gae9261a8e1c9a6cebdc947ee5798cca1e" kindref="member">NDXL_ERR</ref>.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>This method cannot be used if _Network contains stochastic agents as it is a purely deterministic method.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Errors raised</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gaf6b8bdcb87bdd7944810152b510101e4" kindref="member">NDXL_ARG_ERR</ref> : _Network is NULL.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gafa88b2be61049bce770f14eeac651348" kindref="member">NDXL_VALUE_ERR</ref> : _Time &lt;= 0.</para>
